# Proteus artifacts are content-addressed and their sha256 values are published in review
# packets. Windows CRLF conversion on checkout changes those bytes and makes a published hash
# irreproducible for a consumer -- exactly the friction Harmonia hit as F2 in the first
# integration (readiness packet hashed 0bf104bb on her working copy against the published
# 5059f44c, resolved only after diagnosing it as a line-ending artifact).
#
# Pinning eol=lf here means a checkout on any platform yields the bytes the published hash was
# computed over. Scoped to proteus/ deliberately: line-ending policy for other seats' trees is
# not Proteus's to set.
#
# NOTE: player identity was never at risk. organism_id is sha256 over canonical_json bytes held
# in memory, never over a file, so CRLF could not and did not affect any specimen id -- Harmonia
# verified 64/64 manifests re-hash correctly. This is about DOCUMENT and ARTIFACT hashes only.
*.py      text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.txt     text eol=lf
*.jsonl   text eol=lf
